       The  function ffiilleennoo() examines the argument _s_t_r_e_a_m and returns the in‐
       teger file descriptor used to implement this stream.  The file descrip‐
       tor is still owned by _s_t_r_e_a_m and  will  be  closed  when  ffcclloossee(3)  is
       called.  Duplicate the file descriptor with dduupp(2) before passing it to
       code that might close it.

       For the nonlocking counterpart, see uunnlloocckkeedd__ssttddiioo(3).

